Here's the formal **testsmells.org 19-smell catalog** audit of your integration tests:

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

**Clean tests:** 4 of 7 methods have no detectable smells ✅

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, method `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);  // ← blocks 3 seconds, non-deterministic
```

**Integration calibration:** Even for integration tests, hard sleeps remain a smell (per Spadini et al. 2020) — they cause flakiness and bloat suite duration. Only *polling/retry* patterns are acceptable for async coordination.

**Fix:**
```csharp
// Replace with polling or a synchronization primitive
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
    await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures on slow CI, 3 s wasted per run, false passes if event takes longer.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, method `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** One branch is never exercised (the test inserts a plain `User`, so the `PremiumUser` path is dead code). This hides a gap — if `PremiumUser` logic is broken, no test catches it.

**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", 0.15m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — the dead branch creates the illusion of coverage.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, method `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    // ← no assertions at all
}
```

**Problem:** If `Insert` silently drops rows or corrupts data, this test still passes.

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100% pass rate with zero verification.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`, method `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

4 assertions, none with a message parameter. When one fails in CI, the stack trace points to a line but doesn't explain *intent*.

**Fix:** Add messages to disambiguate:
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated ID should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis in CI logs when a failure occurs.

---

## Smell-Free Patterns ✅

These 4 tests are clean and well-structured:

| Method | Notes |
|--------|-------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused scope |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, single assertion |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count contextually obvious (3 items added), `CollectionAssert` used |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good async pattern, clear assertion |

The in-memory SQLite setup avoids **Mystery Guest** (hermetic, no external dependencies) and all tests share the fixture appropriately (**no General Fixture** smell).

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | 2 min | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | 5 min | Split into two focused test methods |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | 10 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling/retry |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | 3 min | Add message parameters to multi-assert methods |

Fixes 1–3 directly prevent false-pass scenarios or flakiness. Fix 4 is a maintainability improvement.
